  "notes": "しゃぶる means to put something in the mouth and suck, lick, or gnaw on it. It is colloquial and often used in the context of babies, children, or animals.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive)\n- Takes ⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧ for the thing being sucked\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ⟦{指|ゆび}→指：01518_yubi⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧しゃぶる: to suck one's finger (babies/children)\n- ⟦{骨|ほね}→骨：02166_hone⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧しゃぶる: to chew/gnaw on a bone\n- ⟦あめ→飴：00687_ame⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧しゃぶる: to suck on candy\n- ⟦おしゃぶり→おしゃぶり：noentry⟧: pacifier (derived noun)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{舐|な}める→舐める：04399_nameru⟧: to lick (more general, broader use)\n- ⟦{吸|す}う→吸う：04394_suu⟧: to suck, to inhale (liquids, cigarettes, air)\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n⟦{骨|ほね}→骨：02166_hone⟧⟦まで→まで：00490_made⟧しゃぶる means to exploit someone to the bone, squeezing out every last bit of value.",
